        url="https://www.sebi.gov.in",
        text="Futures and options are leveraged contracts, which means a small move in price can wipe out the money you put in — and with futures you can lose more than you invested. SEBI's own studies of individual traders found that the large majority (around nine in ten) lost money in F&O, and losses were bigger once costs and taxes were counted. Profits are taxed as business income. It is not a way to build wealth for beginners, and it is certainly not a shortcut to quick income. If you still want to try, use only a small amount you can afford to lose entirely, never borrowed money, and avoid anyone who sells 'sure-shot' F&O calls or paid tips.",
